==Description==
The '''Korblox Seeker''' was an enemy that appeared in [[The Hunt: Mega Edition Event]]. It also appears in [[The Classic Event]] missions as part of [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode. It has a low amount of health and an average speed. On certain waves, it can spawn as a [[Bloated]] and [[Nimble]] enemy.

==Logbook Description==
"''After General Garam demanded peace among all 13 tribes, the Necroborn and Frost Flame Tribe collaborated to create the Korblox Seeker. The Necroborn raised the skeleton of a fallen Redcliff Cadet from the dead and imbued it with the Frost Flame's high resistances. Seekers will travel beyond the empire's territory to gather intelligence on their enemies.''"

==Appearance==
The '''Korblox Seeker''' has blue skin. It wears a black shirt, pants and hood. It has an arm-pad and knee-pad on its right arm and leg, with some blue neon spikes. It does not have a left arm and leg, exposing its skeleton.

==Event Strategy==
As this enemy only appears through [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode, no strategy section is made for its current version. Instead, a strategy section for the one that appeared without [[Sandbox Mode|Sandbox]] mode in [[Korblox Temple]] is listed instead.
*Because of its low health and high amount of cash obtained in the map, multiple early game towers like the [[Militant]], [[Shotgunner]], [[Medic]], [[Electroshocker]] and [[Brawler]] can be used to deal with this.
*As [[Korblox Temple]] gives a lot of cash per wave, high DPS towers like the [[Turret]], [[Accelerator]], [[Pursuit]] or [[Golden Minigunner]] can easily be afforded to deal with this, though this is not necessary as early-game towers on their own can deal with them just fine.

